SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Notes (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Wed. Dec. 9 · 9:00 PM–9:30 PM · Robinson Center\nMANDATOR
 Y — production week. BA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check
 -in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nIn Performance 
 Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named
 . SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails an
 d the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com
 /spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME
  / HAIR / MAKEUP for Archangels: Angels - Archangels — Costume (you pr
 ovide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink
  Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFu
 ll Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and powder 
 matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n
 •  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye shad
 ow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara
  to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeline
 r after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty
  so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  Brown
  or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or 
 eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDan
 cers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nC
 ostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while c
 hanging to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify B
 allet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\
 , no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories
  on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrai
 n from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to 
 alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Neve
 r apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to refr
 ain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain
  from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Neve
 r wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or
  consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water
 \n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or f
 rom the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head piece
 s and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their a
 ssigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Ar
 kansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colo
 red drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
